  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Because invites/requests require that you are in-game for people to be able to send them to you it is completely pointless for them to sent over push notifications when the app isn't even open. Because I am signed in on my phone, while I am playing on PC, I come back to my phone and the notifications are full of past invites/requests. Not only should the app be cleaning these up as they are answered in-game, it should also not be sending this type of notification in the first place since you must be in-game anyways to answer them.\n\nAlso if note is that the \"manage push notifications\" button in the native UI does nothing, and all notifications are under the category \"miscellaneous\" in android, so there is no way to manage this myself.",
